.TH POWERGOV 8 "July 2026" "powergov 1.11.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
powergov \- systemd service for modular laptop power management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B systemctl
.RB [ COMMAND ]
.B powergov.service
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B powergov.service
is a
.BR systemd (8)
unit that starts
.BR powergov (1)
at boot. The daemon evaluates CPU load every two seconds (with 200 ms sampling
for utilization), reads battery/AC state from
.IR /sys/class/power_supply/ ,
computes an effective policy from user mode and hardware context, and applies
changes only when the policy differs from the previous tick.
.PP
On start, configuration is loaded from
.IR /etc/powergov.conf .
Runtime changes via
.BR "powergov mode" ,
.BR "powergov feature" ,
the GTK UI, or
.B powergov \-\-battery-safe
are persisted to that file when handled by the running daemon.
.PP
On graceful shutdown (SIGTERM), the daemon restores CPU frequency caps,
PCI/USB runtime PM settings, and peripheral PM state it modified.
.SH INSTALLATION
.TP
.B sudo make install-service
Installs the binary, configuration template, systemd unit, shell completions,
and manual pages. Enables and starts the service.
.PP
For desktop users, the
.B PowerGov AppImage
can install the same backend after a one-time administrator password prompt.
.SH UNIT FILE
Installed as
.IR /etc/systemd/system/powergov.service .
.PP
Key properties:
.TP
.B ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/powergov on
Foreground daemon process managed by systemd.
.TP
.B Nice=10
Low CPU scheduling priority for the management daemon itself.
.TP
.B RuntimeDirectory=powergov
Creates
.I /run/powergov
for pidfile, socket, and metrics.
.TP
.B LogsDirectory=powergov
Creates
.I /var/log/powergov
for developer logging.
.TP
.B Restart=on-failure
Restarts the daemon if it exits unexpectedly.
.TP
.B WantedBy=multi-user.target
Starts on multi-user boot target.
.SH SUBSYSTEMS
The service may manage, depending on
.IR /etc/powergov.conf
features and user mode:
.TP
.B CPU
Governor, EPP, frequency cap, turbo boost.
.TP
.B Platform
ACPI
.I platform_profile
when power-profiles-daemon is not active.
.TP
.B runtime_pm
PCI and USB
.I power/control
(auto suspend).
.TP
.B disk_pm
Disk APM (hdparm), SATA ALPM, NVMe runtime — level from
.B device_aggression .
.TP
.B pcie_aspm
PCIe ASPM module policy (
.I default
or
.IR powersave ).
.TP
.B bluetooth_pm
Bluetooth HCI runtime power when aggression ≥2 on battery.
.TP
.B peripheral_pm
WiFi (iw) and audio codec power_save.
.SH INTERACTION WITH OTHER TOOLS
If
.B power-profiles-daemon
(GNOME/KDE) is active, powergov automatically disables ACPI
platform_profile
control to avoid conflicting writes. CPU, EPP, turbo, and runtime PM features
remain active unless disabled via configuration.
.PP
If
.B TLP
(service, runtime directory, or active
.BR tlp (8)
stack) is detected, powergov skips
.B runtime_pm ,
.B peripheral_pm ,
.B disk_pm ,
.B pcie_aspm ,
and
.B bluetooth_pm
application to avoid duplicate device policy. CPU and platform features may
still run; for full device PM use powergov without TLP (see
.IR Documentation/operacion.md ).
.PP
Third-party tools such as
.BR cpupower (1)
may overlap with governor and turbo control; use only one primary owner.
.SH SERVICE MANAGEMENT
.TP
.B systemctl start powergov
Start the service.
.TP
.B systemctl stop powergov
Stop gracefully (SIGTERM, restore partial state).
.TP
.B systemctl enable powergov
Enable at boot (done by
.BR make install-service ).
.TP
.B systemctl disable powergov
Disable at boot.
.TP
.B systemctl status powergov
Show unit state and journal output.
.TP
.B make service-status
Convenience wrapper for
.BR systemctl status .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/powergov.service
systemd unit file.
.TP
.I /etc/powergov.conf
Service configuration.
.TP
.I /run/powergov/powergov.pid
Daemon pidfile.
.TP
.I /run/powergov/powergov.sock
Control socket for
.BR powergov (1)
and
.BR powergov-ui .
.TP
.I /run/powergov/metrics
Developer metrics snapshot.
.TP
.I /var/log/powergov/powergov.log
Developer log (when enabled).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR powergov (1),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR systemd.unit (5),
.BR tlp (8),
project documentation in
.IR Documentation/README.md .
